        "source": "import triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n@triton.jit\ndef softmax_fused(X, Y, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    offs = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    col = offs\n    mask = col < N\n    x = tl.load(X + row * N + col, mask, other=-float('inf'))\n    mx = tl.max(x, 0)\n    exps = tl.exp(x - mx)\n    denom = tl.sum(exps, 0)\n    out = exps / denom\n    tl.store(Y + row * N + col, out, mask)\n",
        "rationale": "The original fused kernel failed due to the use of tl.arange with a non-power-of-2 size, which is unsupported. The fix is to round up the BLOCK size argument to the next power of two (here 1024 > 781) and mask out invalid lanes on loads and stores. This preserves the contiguous load/store pattern and full-row processing per program ID, eliminating intermediate buffers and kernel launches, reducing latency and memory usage. Masking ensures correctness on boundary elements. This approach maintains the fusion benefits while resolving the compilation error caused by tl.arange's range restriction."
      },
